00:26:34.793 --> 00:26:36.995
I would say they're bad actors.

00:26:36.995 --> 00:26:40.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the average genderless
person on Twitter

00:26:40.131 --> 00:26:41.800 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think is just
being, 19-year-old,

00:26:41.800 --> 00:26:42.968
is just being used by them.

00:26:42.968 --> 00:26:45.537
- So I think my stance on that

00:26:45.537 --> 00:26:48.440 align:start size:97% position:3%
is what I always assume
people are telling the truth,

00:26:48.440 --> 00:26:50.675
even if I suspect they're not.

00:26:50.675 --> 00:26:52.510 align:start position:0%
I know that sounds
contradictory, but I'll explain.

00:26:52.510 --> 00:26:54.746
The reason for that is I
think part of the problem

00:26:54.746 --> 00:26:56.481 align:start size:84% position:16%
that we have with
political discussion

00:26:56.481 --> 00:26:57.849 align:start size:88% position:13%
and debate and
discourse at the moment

00:26:57.849 --> 00:26:59.050 align:start size:81% position:19%
is that everyone's
just imagining

00:26:59.050 --> 00:27:00.318 align:start size:84% position:16%
what the other
person is thinking,

00:27:00.318 --> 00:27:01.753 align:start size:84% position:16%
and they're arguing
against that.

00:27:01.753 --> 00:27:03.254 align:start size:97% position:3%
So in effect, they're
arguing against themselves.

00:27:03.254 --> 00:27:05.123
So, what I say is, well, look,

00:27:05.123 --> 00:27:07.125 align:start position:0%
if you can defeat the argument,
the argument is defeated,

00:27:07.125 --> 00:27:09.060
irrespective of whether
they mean it or not.

00:27:09.060 --> 00:27:10.562
So just focus on that.

00:27:10.562 --> 00:27:12.097 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, Linda
Sarsour's argument,

00:27:12.097 --> 00:27:13.832
she comes across as quite
an unpleasant individual,

00:27:13.832 --> 00:27:16.434
and I'm sure that maybe she
has got some bad potentially,

00:27:16.434 --> 00:27:18.670 align:start size:97% position:3%
but I'm not gonna assume that,
because I could be wrong.

00:27:18.670 --> 00:27:19.938
I really could be
wrong about that,

00:27:19.938 --> 00:27:21.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know.
- Well, yeah, you're good.

00:27:21.206 --> 00:27:23.008
- Well, okay, fine, but
