00:30:56.120 --> 00:30:57.222
"There's no way we're
gonna reverse this.

00:30:57.222 --> 00:30:59.123
"This is gonna happen."

00:30:59.123 --> 00:31:01.593
And actually, as it happened
they all did try eventually,

00:31:01.593 --> 00:31:03.595 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I think it's that process
of convincing yourself

00:31:03.595 --> 00:31:05.029
that people were misinformed,

00:31:05.029 --> 00:31:08.333 align:start size:97% position:3%
that they just did what
Russian bots told them to do.

00:31:08.333 --> 00:31:09.667 align:start size:84% position:16%
You have the same
over here with Trump.

00:31:09.667 --> 00:31:11.269 align:start size:97% position:3%
You have people--
- Almost everything that I say

00:31:11.269 --> 00:31:12.837 align:start size:84% position:16%
is from--
- A Russian bot, okay.

00:31:12.837 --> 00:31:14.072
- Given to me originally
by a Russian bot, yeah.

00:31:14.072 --> 00:31:16.541
- It's a really lazy
thing which people do

00:31:16.541 --> 00:31:18.042
when they don't wanna
deal with the fact

00:31:18.042 --> 00:31:19.978 align:start size:84% position:16%
that some people
don't agree with them.

00:31:19.978 --> 00:31:21.246 align:start size:84% position:16%
You can't run a
democracy that way.

00:31:21.246 --> 00:31:22.814
One of the things that
frightens me the most,

00:31:22.814 --> 00:31:24.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's happened over
here as well, as you know,

00:31:24.816 --> 00:31:26.451
is that this thing of
the loser's consent

00:31:26.451 --> 00:31:27.919
isn't really present anymore.

00:31:29.320 --> 00:31:32.557 align:start size:97% position:3%
We have to have a situation
in a democratic society

00:31:32.557 --> 00:31:34.325
where we come to
terms with the fact

00:31:34.325 --> 00:31:36.227 align:start size:97% position:3%
that a substantial
proportion of the population

00:31:36.227 --> 00:31:38.296 align:start size:97% position:3%
are going to be led by
people they did not vote for,

00:31:38.296 --> 00:31:39.697
and we all accept that.

00:31:39.697 --> 00:31:40.899 align:start size:84% position:16%
If we lose, we have
to accept that.

00:31:40.899 --> 00:31:42.700 align:start size:84% position:16%
- It's like the most
important thing.

00:31:42.700 --> 00:31:46.771
- It's so important, and
that's been led astray.

00:31:46.771 --> 00:31:51.743
And I think that's to do with
this social justice mentality.

00:31:52.944 --> 00:31:54.212
I'm very aware when
I talk about this,

00:31:54.212 --> 00:31:55.446
'cause social justice
sounds so wonderful

00:31:55.446 --> 00:31:56.381 align:start size:84% position:16%
and it sounds like
I'm knocking something

00:31:56.381 --> 00:31:57.315
that's really good.

00:31:57.315 --> 00:31:58.883
Same with the woke word.

00:31:58.883 --> 00:32:00.385
The word woke comes from the
black civil rights movement,

00:32:00.385 --> 00:32:02.887
and I actually see that
that was appropriated

00:32:02.887 --> 00:32:03.688
by these people.

00:32:04.589 --> 00:32:05.723
The black civil rights movement,

00:32:05.723 --> 00:32:07.191 align:start size:84% position:16%
the gay rights
movement in the '60s,

00:32:07.191 --> 00:32:09.894
the new left, the feminist
movement, that was all great,

00:32:09.894 --> 00:32:12.230
and they knew that free
speech was important.

00:32:12.230 --> 00:32:13.898
And this lot come
along, and they try

00:32:13.898 --> 00:32:16.834 align:start size:97% position:3%
and unpick all of that stuff,
undo it all, reverse it.

00:32:16.834 --> 00:32:18.736
That's why I call
them reactionaries,

00:32:18.736 --> 00:32:20.171
'cause that's what it means.

00:32:20.171 --> 00:32:21.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
It means that you're
uncomfortable with change.

00:32:21.472 --> 00:32:22.707 align:start size:81% position:19%
And that's the
word that's thrown

00:32:22.707 --> 00:32:24.342
at people like us all the time.

00:32:24.342 --> 00:32:26.044 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's them, they're the ones
that are uncomfortable.

00:32:26.044 --> 00:32:27.211
They're the ones that think

00:32:27.211 --> 00:32:28.746 align:start size:84% position:16%
the civil right
movement got it wrong.

00:32:28.746 --> 00:32:31.849
- Right, well, even now you
could just see on MLK Day,

00:32:31.849 --> 00:32:34.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
they start turning on
the things that MLK said.

00:32:34.519 --> 00:32:37.088
This idea that you
should judge people

00:32:37.088 --> 00:32:38.756
on the content of
their character,

00:32:38.756 --> 00:32:41.726
that doesn't really work
in the woke calculator.

00:32:41.726 --> 00:32:44.896
- How long before they
completely deplatform MLK

00:32:44.896 --> 00:32:46.531
or cancel him, I wonder?

00:32:46.531 --> 00:32:48.633 align:start size:97% position:3%
I've got a bit in the new
Titania book I've just written

00:32:48.633 --> 00:32:50.902
where she rewrites his
"I Have a Dream" speech,

00:32:50.902 --> 00:32:52.437
(Dave laughing)

00:32:52.437 --> 00:32:53.871
'cause she wants it to be
about intersectionality.

00:32:53.871 --> 00:32:55.373 align:start position:0%
She wants it to be about
judging the color of your skin,

00:32:55.373 --> 00:32:56.708 align:start size:81% position:19%
not the content
of your character.

00:32:56.708 --> 00:32:58.676 align:start size:97% position:3%
She wants to--
- He was a bigot, that guy.

00:32:58.676 --> 00:33:01.179 align:start position:0%
- Right, exactly, well,
self-hated black man, that's it.

00:33:01.179 --> 00:33:03.915
it's internalized
racism, I guess.

00:33:03.915 --> 00:33:07.318
- Do you think that some
of this is starting to turn

00:33:07.318 --> 00:33:10.955 align:start size:84% position:16%
partly through comedy
and through art?

00:33:10.955 --> 00:33:13.358
We mocked the "Star Wars,"
"Avengers" version of this,

00:33:13.358 --> 00:33:18.062
but your national hero, J.K.
Rowling, did put up a tweet

00:33:18.062 --> 00:33:21.899 align:start size:88% position:13%
that had a certain
anti-diversity message.

00:33:21.899 --> 00:33:23.401
- Yeah, but did you
see the backlash?

00:33:23.401 --> 00:33:24.635
(laughing)

00:33:24.635 --> 00:33:25.570
- So can you tell
the good people

00:33:25.570 --> 00:33:26.771
about what happened there?

00:33:26.771 --> 00:33:28.406 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Yes, so what happened
was there's a woman

00:33:28.406 --> 00:33:30.808
called Maya Forstater who was...

00:33:30.808 --> 00:33:32.343
There was a tribunal in the UK

00:33:32.343 --> 00:33:34.412 align:start size:88% position:13%
because she'd been
dismissed from her work

00:33:34.412 --> 00:33:37.115
because of some tweets she'd
sent or Facebook posts I think,

00:33:37.115 --> 00:33:38.616 align:start size:84% position:16%
where she basically
said that she believes

00:33:38.616 --> 00:33:39.817
that you cannot change sex.

00:33:39.817 --> 00:33:41.486 align:start size:84% position:16%
She thinks that
biology is immutable

00:33:41.486 --> 00:33:44.022
and that we have immutable
biological characteristics,

00:33:44.022 --> 00:33:45.890
which is her opinion and she
has the right to that opinion.

00:33:45.890 --> 00:33:48.526
- And her point was not to
disrespect trans people.

00:33:48.526 --> 00:33:49.761
She was just...

00:33:49.761 --> 00:33:51.195
We go through this
every freakin' week.

00:33:51.195 --> 00:33:52.663
(laughing)

00:33:52.663 --> 00:33:53.998 align:start size:97% position:3%
But all she was just saying
is that biology exists.

00:33:53.998 --> 00:33:55.133
- Right, sure.

00:33:55.133 --> 00:33:56.367 align:start size:84% position:16%
- That was in essence
what she said.

00:33:56.367 --> 00:33:57.368 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Well, it's like
what Blair White said,

00:33:57.368 --> 00:33:58.403
if there is no biological sex,

00:33:58.403 --> 00:33:59.937
there's no such thing as trans.

00:34:02.807 --> 00:34:04.942 align:start size:97% position:3%
Irrespective of the people
being angry about her opinion,

00:34:04.942 --> 00:34:06.811
it was the fact that she
was fired that was scary.

00:34:06.811 --> 00:34:08.780
And then it was the fact
that a judge in the UK

00:34:08.780 --> 00:34:10.481 align:start size:97% position:3%
said that that was not
something you were allowed,

00:34:10.481 --> 00:34:11.849 align:start size:84% position:16%
that you could
legitimately be fired

00:34:11.849 --> 00:34:13.051
for saying something like that.

00:34:13.051 --> 00:34:15.086
So that's what's a
bit scary about that.

00:34:15.086 --> 00:34:16.454
So J.K. Rowling merely tweeted

00:34:16.454 --> 00:34:17.989 align:start size:84% position:16%
and said, "I
support this woman."

00:34:17.989 --> 00:34:19.524 align:start size:88% position:13%
She was saying you
should be able to sleep

00:34:19.524 --> 00:34:20.992
with whoever you want and
identify however you want,

00:34:20.992 --> 00:34:22.293
the liberal position.

00:34:22.293 --> 00:34:23.628
- And she's a lefty.

00:34:23.628 --> 00:34:25.163 align:start size:97% position:3%
- And she's a lefty, right.
- She's a lefty,

00:34:25.163 --> 00:34:26.364
her whole life, J.K., yeah.
- And I think on this stuff,

00:34:26.364 --> 00:34:27.899 align:start size:84% position:16%
you've gotta take
the liberal position,

00:34:27.899 --> 00:34:30.134
which is anyone has the right
to identify however they like

00:34:30.134 --> 00:34:31.369
to live their life however,

00:34:31.369 --> 00:34:32.570
to call themselves
whatever they want.

00:34:32.570 --> 00:34:34.038 align:start size:84% position:16%
What they don't
have the right to do

00:34:34.038 --> 00:34:35.773 align:start size:97% position:3%
is to demand that someone
else calls them those things,

00:34:35.773 --> 00:34:38.242 align:start size:88% position:13%
to monitor and police
someone else's language.

00:34:38.242 --> 00:34:40.478 align:start position:0%
If I get married to my
boyfriend, and I say to someone,

00:34:40.478 --> 00:34:42.346 align:start size:88% position:13%
"I want you to call
this person my husband,"

00:34:42.346 --> 00:34:43.548 align:start size:97% position:3%
but they're a Christian
fundamentalist and they say,

00:34:43.548 --> 00:34:44.882
"I don't recognize
that, I'm not gonna,"

00:34:44.882 --> 00:34:46.384
I can't force that
person to do so.

00:34:46.384 --> 00:34:47.852
I can argue with them,
I can explain to them

00:34:47.852 --> 00:34:50.321 align:start size:97% position:3%
why I think it would be
polite, and that's my right,

00:34:50.321 --> 00:34:52.290 align:start size:97% position:3%
but it's their right, totally
legitimately their right,

00:34:52.290 --> 00:34:54.092 align:start size:84% position:16%
not to do so.
- So the best thing

00:34:54.092 --> 00:34:55.560
wouldn't be to call them a Nazi

00:34:55.560 --> 00:34:57.161
and then try to get the state
power to put them in jail?

00:34:57.161 --> 00:34:58.996 align:start size:81% position:19%
- It's weird, it's
not persuasive.

00:34:58.996 --> 00:34:59.831
It's so weird though, isn't it?

00:34:59.831 --> 00:35:00.932
I don't know why.

00:35:00.932 --> 00:35:02.100
(laughing)

00:35:02.100 --> 00:35:04.368 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's not a good
strategic thing to do,

00:35:04.368 --> 00:35:06.604 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I think we've learned
that over the past few years.

00:35:06.604 --> 00:35:10.041
- We have, but all right, so
J.K. basically offers a defense

00:35:10.041 --> 00:35:11.375
of what this woman said,

00:35:11.375 --> 00:35:13.644 align:start size:97% position:3%
and then go mob.
- Everyone goes mad, right.

00:35:13.644 --> 00:35:15.847 align:start size:84% position:16%
Everyone goes mad
because everyone said
she's a transphobe,

00:35:15.847 --> 00:35:17.248
which she absolutely is not.

00:35:18.416 --> 00:35:21.385
And also she committed
the cardinal sin, right?

00:35:21.385 --> 00:35:25.089 align:start size:97% position:3%
So you know that artists,
particularly one way inclined,

00:35:25.089 --> 00:35:27.158
there's a kind of very
homogenous group think

00:35:27.158 --> 00:35:30.027
amongst artists, amongst
comedians particularly,

00:35:30.027 --> 00:35:33.064
and you get a lot of flack
if you don't quite subscribe

00:35:33.064 --> 00:35:35.199
to those ideas, and she did.

00:35:35.199 --> 00:35:37.301 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's why I don't
think it's going to be

00:35:37.301 --> 00:35:39.504
from art and creatives
that this thing changes,

00:35:39.504 --> 00:35:41.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they're part of
the problem, to be honest.

00:35:41.873 --> 00:35:43.908 align:start size:84% position:16%
I don't think it is
gonna come from there.

00:35:43.908 --> 00:35:46.410
- But when you see like Ricky
Gervais at the Golden Globes,

00:35:46.410 --> 00:35:49.680 align:start size:84% position:16%
where he just scorched
everything that
this book is about

00:35:49.680 --> 00:35:51.682
and the hypocrisy of Hollywood

00:35:51.682 --> 00:35:54.852
and just all of the awful
ideas of intersectionality

00:35:54.852 --> 00:35:56.320
and all of those things,

00:35:57.522 --> 00:35:58.756
that's gotta give
you a little hope.

00:35:58.756 --> 00:36:00.258 align:start size:84% position:16%
- But it does, I mean,
that was brilliant,

00:36:00.258 --> 00:36:03.261
but that's because he's in a
position to do what he wants.

00:36:03.261 --> 00:36:06.030 align:start size:97% position:3%
When he did that speech, there
were a lot of even comics,

00:36:06.030 --> 00:36:07.965
even famous left-wing
comics in the country,

00:36:07.965 --> 00:36:10.468
were saying, "Oh, he's
now like a right-wing,"

00:36:10.468 --> 00:36:11.936
literally calling
him right-wing,

00:36:11.936 --> 00:36:13.804 align:start size:97% position:3%
saying he's a right-wing, he's
part of the establishment.

00:36:13.804 --> 00:36:15.673
These are the very same
people that 10 years ago

00:36:15.673 --> 00:36:18.009
would have cheered him
attacking the hypocrisy

00:36:18.009 --> 00:36:21.045
of the most pampered people
on the planet, let's face it,

00:36:21.045 --> 00:36:22.847
and he was there to do that job.

00:36:22.847 --> 00:36:24.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
But to call that
right-wing is depressing.

00:36:24.949 --> 00:36:27.852
No, I don't think it's gonna
come from artists and creative.

00:36:27.852 --> 00:36:31.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
He can do that because
he's answerable to no one.

00:36:31.122 --> 00:36:33.491
He's in that enviable position.

00:36:33.491 --> 00:36:35.893 align:start size:97% position:3%
But if you're working a
normal job, you can't do that.

00:36:35.893 --> 00:36:37.828
You can't say these things.

00:36:37.828 --> 00:36:39.530
It isn't about state censorship.

00:36:39.530 --> 00:36:41.032
It's about self-censorship.

00:36:41.032 --> 00:36:42.333
It's about the fact that
people feel really nervous

00:36:42.333 --> 00:36:44.035 align:start size:81% position:19%
about what they
say at the moment.

00:36:45.670 --> 00:36:46.971 align:start size:88% position:13%
I wish I could, I
don't want to speak ill

00:36:46.971 --> 00:36:48.206
of artists and stuff
'cause I love them

00:36:48.206 --> 00:36:50.875
and I have an ingrain
respect for anyone

00:36:50.875 --> 00:36:52.410
who wants to create something,

00:36:52.410 --> 00:36:55.213
but I think they're
part of the problem,

00:36:55.213 --> 00:36:56.914
rather than the solution.

00:36:56.914 --> 00:36:59.517
- Do you think that gay
men, for some reason,

00:36:59.517 --> 00:37:02.153
have a unique position in
standing up to this thing?

00:37:03.254 --> 00:37:04.655
You know what I mean?

00:37:04.655 --> 00:37:05.923 align:start size:97% position:3%
It seems to me that
there's a series of people.

00:37:05.923 --> 00:37:08.226
You're going on tour
with Douglas Murray.

00:37:08.226 --> 00:37:10.394
For the first year that I
had read Douglas' stuff,

00:37:10.394 --> 00:37:11.562
I didn't even know he was gay.

00:37:11.562 --> 00:37:13.064
Now we've become good friends,

00:37:13.064 --> 00:37:16.567
and he's truly out there
talking about this stuff,

00:37:16.567 --> 00:37:18.169
and he does a really
interesting dissection

00:37:18.169 --> 00:37:22.006
of why you should separate
the T from the LGBT thing,

00:37:23.441 --> 00:37:26.477
but it does seem to me that
there's a bunch of gay men

00:37:26.477 --> 00:37:28.479
that are sort of leading
the fight against this.

00:37:28.479 --> 00:37:30.881
Do you think there's
a reason for that?

00:37:30.881 --> 00:37:32.416
- Well, there's the
conflict I think

00:37:32.416 --> 00:37:34.418
between certain elements of
the extreme trans ideology,

00:37:34.418 --> 00:37:36.621
which just doesn't sit
well with gay rights,

00:37:38.022 --> 00:37:42.593
because they would say that you
can't be same-sex attracted,

00:37:43.794 --> 00:37:45.263
right, and because they
don't wanna see biology.

00:37:45.263 --> 00:37:48.132 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that's a
problem for gay men.

00:37:48.132 --> 00:37:50.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think there is that
fundamental problem there.

00:37:50.067 --> 00:37:53.037
Also, I think it comes
from freedom of thought.

00:37:53.037 --> 00:37:55.139
I think a lotta gay people,

00:37:55.139 --> 00:37:56.774
particularly maybe
slightly the older,

00:37:56.774 --> 00:38:01.712 align:start position:0%
maybe the X generation, you
did have to think for yourself.

00:38:02.913 --> 00:38:03.714
A lot of gay people
who were growing up

00:38:03.714 --> 00:38:04.882
when I was growing up,

00:38:04.882 --> 00:38:05.683 align:start size:84% position:16%
they ended up in
straight relationships

00:38:05.683 --> 00:38:06.917
and straight marriages,

00:38:06.917 --> 00:38:08.119
but the ones who could
think for themselves

00:38:08.119 --> 00:38:10.154 align:start size:84% position:16%
and think outside
the box were the ones

00:38:10.154 --> 00:38:11.355
who embraced who they were.

00:38:11.355 --> 00:38:12.857
- Wait, that's interesting.

00:38:12.857 --> 00:38:14.792
So a lotta gay people that
you knew maybe 20 years ago

00:38:14.792 --> 00:38:16.927 align:start size:88% position:13%
ended up in
heterosexual marriages.

00:38:16.927 --> 00:38:17.862
- Yeah, some did.

00:38:18.996 --> 00:38:20.765 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Meaning that they
became straight

00:38:20.765 --> 00:38:23.034
or meaning that they
just couldn't fight

00:38:23.034 --> 00:38:26.771 align:start size:84% position:16%
the idea of normalcy
or something.

00:38:26.771 --> 00:38:28.306 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Well, you know back then,
it was a very different world.

00:38:28.306 --> 00:38:30.775 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean, everything about
society did coach you

00:38:30.775 --> 00:38:34.879
to be straight, and you did
just assume that you were.

00:38:36.314 --> 00:38:38.382
And so I think it takes
a certain kind of mindset

00:38:38.382 --> 00:38:39.984
to understand that
actually you're not,

00:38:39.984 --> 00:38:41.686
to accept that you're not.

00:38:41.686 --> 00:38:42.953
Very different now,

00:38:42.953 --> 00:38:44.855
we live in a totally
different world now.

00:38:44.855 --> 00:38:47.491 align:start size:97% position:3%
Everything's completely
equal and everything's fine.

00:38:47.491 --> 00:38:48.759
Yeah, I do know some people.

00:38:48.759 --> 00:38:50.227
I don't wanna name
names (laughing),

00:38:50.227 --> 00:38:52.196 align:start size:97% position:3%
but I know some people who
are in straight relationships,

00:38:52.196 --> 00:38:54.932
but they're not really
insofar as they double.

00:38:56.133 --> 00:38:58.536
And I think it's just
a generational thing.

00:38:58.536 --> 00:39:01.172
- Yeah, well, plus now
we were in "Endgame"

00:39:01.172 --> 00:39:03.774
with that guy, the psychologist.

00:39:03.774 --> 00:39:04.709 align:start position:0%
- [Andrew] I have to say I
haven't actually seen "Endgame."

00:39:04.709 --> 00:39:05.943
- Oh, you haven't seen it?

00:39:05.943 --> 00:39:07.111 align:start size:81% position:19%
Literally, it's
the most pathetic,

00:39:07.111 --> 00:39:08.746 align:start size:88% position:13%
they're sitting in
like a self-help group,

00:39:08.746 --> 00:39:11.549
and this one guy is
like, "I survived"

00:39:12.717 --> 00:39:14.352
what happened at the end
of the "Infinity War."

00:39:14.352 --> 00:39:17.288
"I survived it, and
I went on a date."

00:39:17.288 --> 00:39:20.291 align:start position:0%
And then Captain America's
like, "Oh god, it's wonderful."

00:39:20.291 --> 00:39:22.426 align:start size:88% position:13%
- I don't like superhero
films, firstly,

00:39:22.426 --> 00:39:23.627
so I'm gonna put that out there.

00:39:23.627 --> 00:39:24.795 align:start size:84% position:16%
But also, I just
think they're silly.

00:39:24.795 --> 00:39:25.730 align:start size:84% position:16%
They're people flying
around in capes,

00:39:25.730 --> 00:39:27.198
I can't get onboard with that.

00:39:27.198 --> 00:39:28.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like even with Batman,
even in "The Dark Knight,"

00:39:28.399 --> 00:39:29.667 align:start size:88% position:13%
where everyone says
it's really serious art.

00:39:29.667 --> 00:39:30.601
- Oh, that was good.
- It makes me laugh.

00:39:30.601 --> 00:39:31.402 align:start size:72% position:28%
It's silly.
- Yeah?

00:39:31.402 --> 00:39:32.503
- Yeah, it's for kids.

00:39:32.503 --> 00:39:34.538 align:start size:84% position:16%
(laughing) So anyway--
- A gay guy

00:39:34.538 --> 00:39:35.873
who doesn't like capes,

00:39:35.873 --> 00:39:36.974 align:start size:81% position:19%
very bizarre.
- Exactly, I know,

00:39:36.974 --> 00:39:38.309
and I'm Catholic.

00:39:38.309 --> 00:39:39.510
No, but that thing about,

00:39:39.510 --> 00:39:41.145
all I know is I read an article

00:39:41.145 --> 00:39:44.181 align:start size:84% position:16%
in "The Guardian"
about "Endgame," and
it said it was great,

00:39:44.181 --> 00:39:46.050 align:start size:84% position:16%
but the fat-shaming
broke my heart,

00:39:46.050 --> 00:39:47.318
and I just thought, come on.

00:39:47.318 --> 00:39:48.352
- Oh, because Thor was fat.

00:39:48.352 --> 00:39:49.553
- Is there fat-shaming in that?

00:39:49.553 --> 00:39:51.622 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah, they made Thor
fat and, you know.

00:39:51.622 --> 00:39:53.124 align:start size:84% position:16%
- But there's
something quite funny

00:39:53.124 --> 00:39:54.358
about a Norse god letting
himself go, isn't there?

00:39:54.358 --> 00:39:56.193
- Of course, it was, of
course, it was funny.

00:39:56.193 --> 00:39:58.295
But even that, I'm glad you
brought that up actually,

00:39:58.295 --> 00:39:59.797
'cause that's been
popping up lately,

00:39:59.797 --> 00:40:03.467
that now if you say anything
about people that are fat,

00:40:03.467 --> 00:40:05.803 align:start size:84% position:16%
that you're--
- Well, I don't like

00:40:05.803 --> 00:40:08.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
mocking or bullying
someone about their size.

00:40:08.406 --> 00:40:10.074
I think that's really bad.
- But it's like you're almost

00:40:10.074 --> 00:40:11.842 align:start size:81% position:19%
not allowed to
say that being fit

00:40:11.842 --> 00:40:13.577 align:start size:88% position:13%
or eating right or
taking care of yourself

00:40:13.577 --> 00:40:15.813
is actually something
you should aspire to,

00:40:15.813 --> 00:40:17.982 align:start size:88% position:13%
which we all inherently
know is true.

00:40:17.982 --> 00:40:18.916 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Well, that's the problem.
- It doesn't mean

00:40:18.916 --> 00:40:20.418
we all do it all the time.

00:40:20.418 --> 00:40:21.819
- A lot of people had to
go with Cancer Research UK

00:40:21.819 --> 00:40:23.354
which is a charity in the UK.

00:40:23.354 --> 00:40:25.122
They recently put a number
of posters up on the tube

00:40:25.122 --> 00:40:27.224
saying that obesity is
now the highest form,

00:40:27.224 --> 00:40:28.692
the most common form of cancer,

00:40:28.692 --> 00:40:30.127
or the most common
cause of cancer.

00:40:30.127 --> 00:40:31.629
It's actually overtaken smoking.

00:40:31.629 --> 00:40:34.298 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then a lot of social
justice activists went crazy,

00:40:34.298 --> 00:40:35.566 align:start size:84% position:16%
and were saying,
"You're fat-shaming.

00:40:35.566 --> 00:40:37.501 align:start size:84% position:16%
"You're gonna
cause more deaths,"

00:40:37.501 --> 00:40:39.837 align:start size:88% position:13%
and calling them some
really unpleasant words.

00:40:39.837 --> 00:40:41.405
These are good people.

00:40:41.405 --> 00:40:43.474
These are good people who
are trying to help people.

00:40:43.474 --> 00:40:46.577
I think you don't wanna mock

00:40:46.577 --> 00:40:48.846 line:0%
or attack people for their size,

00:40:48.846 --> 00:40:50.681 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
but on the same token,
it's not good to tell kids

00:40:50.681 --> 00:40:52.616 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
it's doesn't matter
what you eat,

00:40:52.616 --> 00:40:54.685 line:0%
it doesn't matter how
overweight you are,

00:40:54.685 --> 00:40:57.354 line:0%
because they're gonna die
younger, like that's it.

00:40:58.789 --> 00:41:01.192 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I think why can't we
just accept medical reality?

00:41:02.259 --> 00:41:03.994 align:start size:88% position:13%
- It's really--
- Am I gonna get accused

00:41:03.994 --> 00:41:05.229
of fat-shaming for saying that?

00:41:05.229 --> 00:41:06.497
- You definitely, no,
no, no, it's very clear

00:41:06.497 --> 00:41:09.099
you're a fataphobe
or a weightaphobe,

00:41:09.099 --> 00:41:09.934
(laughing)

00:41:09.934 --> 00:41:11.135
or something, something.

00:41:11.135 --> 00:41:12.837 align:start size:84% position:16%
So when you first
came out with Titania,

00:41:15.272 --> 00:41:16.507
the character wasn't originally

00:41:16.507 --> 00:41:18.509
associated with
you fully, right?

00:41:18.509 --> 00:41:19.443
- I was in the closet.

00:41:19.443 --> 00:41:20.644
- Yeah, you were in the closet,

00:41:20.644 --> 00:41:22.546 align:start size:88% position:13%
and then you were outed?
- I was outed, yeah.

00:41:22.546 --> 00:41:24.748
- Yeah, can you talk a
little bit about that?

00:41:24.748 --> 00:41:28.185
So you create this character.
- I wanted to be anonymous.

00:41:28.185 --> 00:41:30.154
And it just meant that I was
free to say whatever I want.

00:41:30.154 --> 00:41:31.689
I wasn't worried about it.

00:41:31.689 --> 00:41:34.325
What happened was
I wrote the book,

00:41:34.325 --> 00:41:36.727
and then in the week
that the book came out,

00:41:36.727 --> 00:41:38.429 align:start size:88% position:13%
there was a bit of
press interest about it.

00:41:38.429 --> 00:41:42.066 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so there was a journalist
at "The Sunday Times,"

00:41:42.066 --> 00:41:43.634
Rosamund Urwin I
think her name was,

00:41:43.634 --> 00:41:46.904
who did some investigative
work and sort of dug up...

00:41:46.904 --> 00:41:48.572
She read a lot of my
political articles

00:41:48.572 --> 00:41:50.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she'd read an
advanced copy of the book,

00:41:50.641 --> 00:41:52.943
and she worked out that some
of the quotations were similar.

00:41:52.943 --> 00:41:54.245
It was a really good job.

00:41:54.245 --> 00:41:55.646
- [Dave] Wow, like
a real journalist!

00:41:55.646 --> 00:41:57.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yeah, proper
investigative journalist.

00:41:57.047 --> 00:41:58.582
- So far.

00:41:58.582 --> 00:42:00.017
- And she whittled it down
to me and a friend of mine,

00:42:00.017 --> 00:42:02.653 align:start position:0%
Lisa Graves, who runs a
character called Jarvis Dupont.

00:42:02.653 --> 00:42:03.854
I don't know if you follow him,

00:42:03.854 --> 00:42:04.955 align:start size:84% position:16%
he's a really funny
parody account,

00:42:04.955 --> 00:42:06.891 align:start size:84% position:16%
you should follow him.
- No, okay.

00:42:06.891 --> 00:42:08.492
- Her, sorry, she's
just transitioned.

00:42:08.492 --> 00:42:11.462
(laughing)

00:42:11.462 --> 00:42:13.130
She whittled it down to us,

00:42:13.130 --> 00:42:15.466 align:start size:84% position:16%
and then a comedy
website called Chortle

00:42:15.466 --> 00:42:16.700
found the smoking gun.

00:42:16.700 --> 00:42:19.136
Some sort of a book
festival brochure,

00:42:19.136 --> 00:42:20.337
which accidentally named me.

00:42:20.337 --> 00:42:21.672 align:start size:81% position:19%
It was someone
from the publisher

00:42:21.672 --> 00:42:23.807
accidentally named
me as the author.

00:42:23.807 --> 00:42:25.609 align:start size:97% position:3%
And that happened--
- Wait, when you had signed

00:42:25.609 --> 00:42:27.912
the deal for the book,
did you have assurances

00:42:27.912 --> 00:42:30.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
from your publisher that--
- Just verbal.

00:42:31.682 --> 00:42:32.483
We just decided that
it would be better

00:42:32.483 --> 00:42:33.517
if I didn't come out.

00:42:34.652 --> 00:42:35.786
It just so happened
that it came out

00:42:35.786 --> 00:42:37.421
the week the book was published,

00:42:37.421 --> 00:42:39.490 align:start size:84% position:16%
and that ended up
with a lotta publicity

00:42:39.490 --> 00:42:41.525 align:start size:88% position:13%
as a result of that, and
the story then became

00:42:41.525 --> 00:42:44.762
that it was me who was
behind the character.

00:42:44.762 --> 00:42:47.431
But the only difference
is I've never changed

00:42:47.431 --> 00:42:49.767 align:start size:97% position:3%
the way she speaks, I've
never changed the character,

00:42:49.767 --> 00:42:52.036
I've never censored myself.

00:42:52.036 --> 00:42:54.004 align:start size:97% position:3%
The only difference is that
now whenever I tweet something

00:42:54.004 --> 00:42:55.472
that maybe is a bit contentious,

00:42:55.472 --> 00:42:57.875
I get the attacks,
I get the deluge.

00:42:57.875 --> 00:43:00.377 align:start size:88% position:13%
I had it recently
where I tweeted a joke,

00:43:00.377 --> 00:43:01.712
and it was an anti-racist joke.

00:43:01.712 --> 00:43:03.981
It was mocking a
racist stereotype,

00:43:03.981 --> 00:43:05.816
and people, of course, because
they're very literal-minded,

00:43:05.816 --> 00:43:08.686 align:start size:84% position:16%
interpreted it as
being a racist joke,

00:43:08.686 --> 00:43:10.154
right?
- Mm-hmm.

00:43:10.154 --> 00:43:11.889 align:start size:97% position:3%
- So I got lots of people
attacking me online personally

00:43:11.889 --> 00:43:13.057 align:start size:97% position:3%
and calling me racist and
Nazi and all the rest of it.

00:43:13.057 --> 00:43:14.625
So that's the down side of it.

00:43:14.625 --> 00:43:16.126
- So everything being equal,

00:43:16.126 --> 00:43:19.797
you would have preferred to
have kept these two personas,

00:43:19.797 --> 00:43:21.231
or the human and the persona,

00:43:21.231 --> 00:43:23.901 align:start size:88% position:13%
separate, just for
artistic freedom, right?

00:43:23.901 --> 00:43:25.502
- Yeah, and also, yeah, I would,

00:43:25.502 --> 00:43:27.137 align:start position:0%
and it's nice, it's nice 'cause
you get into a character,

00:43:27.137 --> 00:43:28.606
you start to think like her,

00:43:28.606 --> 00:43:29.873
I started to dream as her.

00:43:29.873 --> 00:43:30.808
(Dave laughing)

00:43:30.808 --> 00:43:32.776
I know this isn't healthy,

00:43:32.776 --> 00:43:36.313
but all of that sort
of stuff, I like that.

00:43:36.313 --> 00:43:37.681
I like the idea of
inventing characters

00:43:37.681 --> 00:43:39.283
and writing behind characters.

00:43:40.484 --> 00:43:41.652
And it also affects
the interpretation,

00:43:41.652 --> 00:43:43.387 align:start size:88% position:13%
because now people
interpret the character

00:43:43.387 --> 00:43:45.155
on the basis of my
personal politics,

00:43:45.155 --> 00:43:46.690
or misinterpret,
as the case may be.

00:43:46.690 --> 00:43:51.128
- Right, so as someone that
at least originally intended

00:43:51.128 --> 00:43:53.430
to be an anonymous
character online,

00:43:53.430 --> 00:43:54.698
that is no longer anonymous,

00:43:54.698 --> 00:43:56.300
what's your take
on just generally,

00:43:56.300 --> 00:43:58.736
like the tenor of what people
talk about on social media

00:43:58.736 --> 00:44:01.505
and how much of it is done
through anonymous accounts?

00:44:01.505 --> 00:44:02.740
- Oh, loads of it is.

00:44:02.740 --> 00:44:04.308 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's why it's such
a cesspit, right?

00:44:06.477 --> 00:44:08.012
The thing about Twitter

00:44:08.012 --> 00:44:10.814
and the thing about all of
that stuff is that people,

00:44:10.814 --> 00:44:12.750 align:start size:88% position:13%
the anonymity frees
them up to be horrible,

00:44:12.750 --> 00:44:14.251
(laughing)

00:44:14.251 --> 00:44:15.586
to be even worse and to say
things that they never would,

00:44:15.586 --> 00:44:16.887
even when they're not anonymous.

00:44:16.887 --> 00:44:18.689
Now, I've had situations
where people have said

00:44:18.689 --> 00:44:20.391
the most horrible things online.

00:44:20.391 --> 00:44:22.693 align:start size:88% position:13%
When you meet them,
it's a different story.

00:44:22.693 --> 00:44:23.961 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Oh, of course.
- They don't wanna...

00:44:23.961 --> 00:44:27.097
So that element of it,
but on the other hand,

00:44:27.097 --> 00:44:28.532 align:start size:88% position:13%
it does enable, I think
you should be able

00:44:28.532 --> 00:44:30.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
to have satirical accounts
and parody accounts

00:44:30.200 --> 00:44:31.435
and all the rest of the stuff.

00:44:31.435 --> 00:44:33.704
So I think it's a good thing.

00:44:33.704 --> 00:44:37.107
- Do you sense now after
the J.K. Rowling thing

00:44:37.107 --> 00:44:39.943 align:start size:97% position:3%
that we discussed and enough
of these conversations,

00:44:39.943 --> 00:44:41.645
what do you sense
would be the thing

00:44:41.645 --> 00:44:45.115
that would need to get
us to the tipping point

00:44:45.115 --> 00:44:46.116
where we start...

00:44:46.116 --> 00:44:47.751
Are we starting to get there?

00:44:47.751 --> 00:44:49.286 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'm sensing that
something's happening,

00:44:49.286 --> 00:44:51.989 align:start size:97% position:3%
I think at least maybe through
the American election now.

00:44:51.989 --> 00:44:53.490 align:start size:84% position:16%
I tweeted at the
beginning of the year

00:44:53.490 --> 00:44:55.859 align:start size:97% position:3%
that this is the year it
implodes because it can't...

00:44:55.859 --> 00:44:57.895
The intersectional
thing can't hold

00:44:57.895 --> 00:44:59.129
for an election like this,

00:44:59.129 --> 00:45:00.464
and it's partly what you said

00:45:00.464 --> 00:45:02.833 align:start size:84% position:16%
about why Jeremy
Corbyn doesn't fit in

00:45:02.833 --> 00:45:04.368
with the intersectional thing.

00:45:04.368 --> 00:45:05.602
I think we have a version
of that with Bernie here.

00:45:05.602 --> 00:45:08.405
- You do, and we know
that intersectional

00:45:08.405 --> 00:45:10.908 align:start size:88% position:13%
identity politics
loses elections, right?

00:45:10.908 --> 00:45:12.576 align:start size:84% position:16%
Mark Lilla wrote about
this in his book,

00:45:12.576 --> 00:45:14.078
"The Once and Future Liberal."

00:45:14.078 --> 00:45:16.413 align:start size:97% position:3%
We know that across the board,
that always happens, right?

00:45:16.413 --> 00:45:18.615
Identity politics,
Hillary Clinton,

00:45:18.615 --> 00:45:19.783
dividing people up
into their gender,

00:45:19.783 --> 00:45:21.285
their race, and everything,

00:45:21.285 --> 00:45:23.687
saying I'm gonna target this
demographic, it doesn't work.

00:45:23.687 --> 00:45:25.222
- And worldwide it doesn't work,

00:45:25.222 --> 00:45:26.423
which is why the
right is winning

00:45:26.423 --> 00:45:27.791
basically everywhere right now.

00:45:27.791 --> 00:45:29.226 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Here's the problem
you have though

00:45:29.226 --> 00:45:32.563 align:start position:0%
is that the intersectional
left, for want of a better term,

00:45:32.563 --> 00:45:33.831
they come up with this premise,

00:45:33.831 --> 00:45:35.499
and their premise
is that they know

00:45:35.499 --> 00:45:37.301 align:start size:97% position:3%
that anyone who is right-wing
is secretly a fascist,

00:45:37.301 --> 00:45:40.037 align:start position:0%
anyone who votes for Donald
Trump is secretly a Nazi, okay?

00:45:40.037 --> 00:45:41.305
So then when he wins,

00:45:41.305 --> 00:45:42.740
they point it out and
say, "That's evidence

00:45:42.740 --> 00:45:44.508 align:start size:97% position:3%
"that our premise was right."
- It's evidence.

00:45:44.508 --> 00:45:49.513
- So after the last one, and I
wrote this Jonathan Pie video

00:45:50.681 --> 00:45:52.516
about the Hillary
Clinton losing,

00:45:52.516 --> 00:45:54.284
and saying it was the left,

00:45:54.284 --> 00:45:56.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
the left need to
reevaluate their position,

00:45:56.820 --> 00:45:59.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
they need to rethink about
the way they're going.

00:45:59.022 --> 00:46:00.624
But they didn't, they double
downed and they made it worse.

00:46:00.624 --> 00:46:02.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
I genuinely at that
point thought they would,

00:46:02.860 --> 00:46:04.394 align:start size:88% position:13%
there would be a period
of self-reflection.

00:46:04.394 --> 00:46:06.330
- I think we all thought it.

00:46:06.330 --> 00:46:07.564
- But what they did
instead is they said,

00:46:07.564 --> 00:46:09.466
"This proves all of
our worst fears."

00:46:09.466 --> 00:46:11.368
It's a circle of
reasoning thing,

00:46:11.368 --> 00:46:15.405 align:start position:0%
and that's why I worry it might
not get better that quickly

00:46:15.405 --> 00:46:17.374
because if Trump wins again,

00:46:17.374 --> 00:46:18.542
which I'm pretty
convinced he will,

00:46:18.542 --> 00:46:19.777 align:start size:84% position:16%
then what will happen
is they'll say,

00:46:19.777 --> 00:46:21.145
they'll take that
as further evidence

00:46:21.145 --> 00:46:23.547
that we live in this
crypto-fascist state,

00:46:23.547 --> 00:46:28.352 align:start size:97% position:3%
and they'll just accelerate
all the crazy mania

00:46:28.352 --> 00:46:29.853
that they've been doing
over the past few years.

00:46:29.853 --> 00:46:31.789
- Do you think our institutions

00:46:31.789 --> 00:46:33.624
are able to stand
up against this?

00:46:33.624 --> 00:46:35.259 align:start size:84% position:16%
So this is sorta what
you hinted before

00:46:35.259 --> 00:46:36.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
about what's happening
with Brexit with you guys,

00:46:36.827 --> 00:46:38.195
but even what we see
out of the left now,

00:46:38.195 --> 00:46:40.097
they wanna get rid of
the electoral college,

00:46:40.097 --> 00:46:41.732 align:start size:84% position:16%
they wanna add Supreme
Court justices,

00:46:41.732 --> 00:46:43.300
they don't want states' rights.

00:46:43.300 --> 00:46:45.669
These are now structural things

00:46:45.669 --> 00:46:47.104
that I think if
Trump wins again,

00:46:47.104 --> 00:46:48.505
which I agree he's going to,

00:46:49.840 --> 00:46:52.276 align:start size:97% position:3%
short of really some
cataclysmic thing happening,

00:46:52.276 --> 00:46:53.911
that what their
move is gonna be,

00:46:53.911 --> 00:46:55.212
well, not only do you
figure out a new way

00:46:55.212 --> 00:46:56.613
to try to impeach him

00:46:56.613 --> 00:46:58.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you just don't
accept elections anymore,

00:46:58.715 --> 00:47:01.819 align:start size:97% position:3%
but it will be to attack
every one of the last vestiges

00:47:01.819 --> 00:47:03.353
of our functioning democracy.

00:47:03.353 --> 00:47:05.789
- I think so, and
that's why I think

00:47:05.789 --> 00:47:08.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
we do need to seriously
consider the tactics here.

00:47:09.660 --> 00:47:11.728
I've gone for the
satirical route.

00:47:13.163 --> 00:47:17.034
I also write argumentative
articles, but let's face it,

00:47:17.034 --> 00:47:19.102
these people aren't really
willing to be persuaded.

00:47:19.102 --> 00:47:21.171
I mean, they often won't turn
up to debates or arguments

00:47:21.171 --> 00:47:22.573
because they don't
want to discuss.

00:47:22.573 --> 00:47:24.041 align:start size:84% position:16%
They see it as--
- But you said to me

00:47:24.041 --> 00:47:25.409
right before we started,
you do something that I do,

00:47:25.409 --> 00:47:27.311
which is that if
someone has a Q&amp;A,

00:47:27.311 --> 00:47:30.047
you try to bring up people
that disagree with you first.

00:47:30.047 --> 00:47:31.215
- That's what I want
more than anything.

00:47:31.215 --> 00:47:33.951 align:start size:84% position:16%
I want the discussion
to be opened up.

00:47:33.951 --> 00:47:35.419
At the moment, it's not.

00:47:35.419 --> 00:47:38.288
So I think tactically,
we have to think about

00:47:38.288 --> 00:47:39.623
setting an example, right?

00:47:39.623 --> 00:47:42.392
So anyone who believes
in freedom and liberty,

00:47:42.392 --> 00:47:44.928
we need to firstly ditch this
guilt by association thing.

00:47:44.928 --> 00:47:48.131
So we need to be able to talk
to people we don't agree with.

00:47:48.131 --> 00:47:51.201 align:start size:84% position:16%
If I appear on a
show, when I appeared

00:47:51.201 --> 00:47:52.703 align:start size:84% position:16%
with Tucker Carlton
