book with illustrations

00:55:17.547 --> 00:55:18.748 align:start size:88% position:13%
and all the rest of it.
- Nice.

00:55:18.748 --> 00:55:20.216 align:start size:88% position:13%
- But it's gonna be
horribly inappropriate.

00:55:20.216 --> 00:55:22.919
- And then you're going on
tour with Mr. Douglas Murray.

00:55:22.919 --> 00:55:25.121 align:start size:84% position:16%
- With Douglas Murray,
which is great.

00:55:25.121 --> 00:55:27.424
So the tour is called
"Resisting Wokeness,"

00:55:27.424 --> 00:55:28.625 align:start size:88% position:13%
which sounds quite
provocative, I suppose,

00:55:28.625 --> 00:55:29.793
but what I really want to do

00:55:29.793 --> 00:55:31.561 align:start size:88% position:13%
is get people to discuss
this stuff, right?

00:55:32.696 --> 00:55:34.731
People are feeling that
they're in a society

00:55:34.731 --> 00:55:36.700
where they don't feel
able or comfortable

00:55:36.700 --> 00:55:39.002 align:start size:88% position:13%
to say what they believe
to be true anymore.

00:55:39.002 --> 00:55:40.937 align:start position:0%
So we want people to come
along and have that discussion,

00:55:40.937 --> 00:55:42.405
and we're gonna
go around the UK,

00:55:42.405 --> 00:55:45.842 align:start size:97% position:3%
we're gonna end up at the
Hammersmith Apollo in London.

00:55:45.842 --> 00:55:47.744
It's basically we're gonna be
talking through the issues,

00:55:47.744 --> 00:55:50.280
trying to actually
work the issues out.

00:55:50.280 --> 00:55:51.514
Even talking to you today,

00:55:51.514 --> 00:55:52.816 align:start size:84% position:16%
there are things that
I'm not clear on,

00:55:52.816 --> 00:55:54.818 align:start size:81% position:19%
and I want to talk
more about it,

00:55:54.818 --> 00:55:57.053
and I'm willing to be persuaded.

00:55:57.053 --> 00:55:58.555
This is the main reason I think

00:55:58.555 --> 00:56:00.690
for talking to people
you don't agree with

00:56:00.690 --> 00:56:01.925
is you might be wrong.

00:56:01.925 --> 00:56:03.360
There are all sorts of
things I'm probably,

00:56:03.360 --> 00:56:04.494
almost certainly wrong about,

00:56:04.494 --> 00:56:05.695
and I wanna know what they are.

00:56:05.695 --> 00:56:07.263
I mean, yeah, you can say...

00:56:07.263 --> 00:56:09.065
I can argue with people
to refine my argument.

00:56:09.065 --> 00:56:10.300
That's a selfish perspective.

00:56:10.300 --> 00:56:11.468
I think it should
be, well, actually,

00:56:11.468 --> 00:56:13.002 align:start size:84% position:16%
it's good to be proven
wrong, isn't it?

00:56:13.002 --> 00:56:14.704
So Douglas and I are gonna
tour, and it's really good

00:56:14.704 --> 00:56:16.039 align:start size:97% position:3%
because we come from different
political backgrounds.

00:56:16.039 --> 00:56:17.807 align:start size:84% position:16%
- [Dave] Yeah, Douglas
is a conservative.

00:56:17.807 --> 00:56:19.075
- He's a conservative and
we have different views

00:56:19.075 --> 00:56:20.243
on all sorts of things.

00:56:20.243 --> 00:56:23.446 align:start size:88% position:13%
On this matter, we
share the same concern.

00:56:23.446 --> 00:56:25.281
I've found it so weird
over the past few years

00:56:25.281 --> 00:56:29.085
that I've made all these new
allies, these new friends.

00:56:29.085 --> 00:56:30.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
- That was where I wanted
to go just for the--

00:56:30.620 --> 00:56:31.588
- Oh, I'm anticipating.

00:56:31.588 --> 00:56:33.156
- No, well, you gotta, really.

00:56:33.156 --> 00:56:34.691
I guess I don't even need
to ask you the question,

00:56:34.691 --> 00:56:38.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
but through all of this
that you have been through

00:56:38.361 --> 00:56:40.697 align:start size:97% position:3%
and writing books, and
being in the Twitter fights,

00:56:40.697 --> 00:56:42.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the world of this, and
talking about something

00:56:42.832 --> 00:56:45.034
that's so culturally relevant,

00:56:45.034 --> 00:56:47.771
are you shocked by the
people on the right?

00:56:49.205 --> 00:56:50.740
'Cause I sometimes
am still shocked

00:56:50.740 --> 00:56:54.344
by how welcoming these
people are, and I still,

00:56:54.344 --> 00:56:57.480 align:start size:84% position:16%
one of the things
that the genderless,

00:56:57.480 --> 00:56:58.681
anonymous people on
Twitter will say,

00:56:58.681 --> 00:57:00.683 align:start size:84% position:16%
"Dave, the right's
being nice to you now,

00:57:00.683 --> 00:57:02.886 align:start size:97% position:3%
"but they're just using you,
they're just using you,"

00:57:02.886 --> 00:57:05.422
as if I'm some sort of
incapacitated moron.

00:57:05.422 --> 00:57:06.856
Do you know what I mean?

00:57:06.856 --> 00:57:08.958 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's like I have no voligent
over my own thoughts.

00:57:08.958 --> 00:57:10.193
- Exactly.

00:57:10.193 --> 00:57:13.329
- And it's like I think
that I have seen great

00:57:13.329 --> 00:57:15.131 align:start size:88% position:13%
intellectual flexibility
with these people.

00:57:15.131 --> 00:57:16.933
I don't agree with
them on everything,

00:57:16.933 --> 00:57:19.536
on abortion and a few other
things, you know what I mean?

00:57:19.536 --> 00:57:21.404 align:start size:84% position:16%
But they're willing
to talk it out.

00:57:21.404 --> 00:57:22.639
(sighs)

00:57:22.639 --> 00:57:24.274 align:start size:84% position:16%
- The truth is that,
the boring truth,

00:57:24.274 --> 00:57:27.911
is that most people
are nice, basically.

00:57:27.911 --> 00:57:29.779
The vast majority of
people are just decent,

00:57:29.779 --> 00:57:32.615
and you've just got the
extremes on both sides

00:57:32.615 --> 00:57:34.818
who discolor the
entire movement,

00:57:34.818 --> 00:57:36.052
whatever movement
they're a part of.

00:57:36.052 --> 00:57:38.521 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's like the trans
activists on the whole

00:57:38.521 --> 00:57:39.956
are decent people.

00:57:39.956 --> 00:57:41.958 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's the minority, the
really angry, violent group

00:57:41.958 --> 00:57:46.029
that just really make it
hard for all the others.

00:57:46.029 --> 00:57:47.630
And so we've got the same thing.

00:57:49.032 --> 00:57:51.034 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'll be honest, because I
come from the comedy circuit,

00:57:51.034 --> 00:57:53.603
so most of my friends have
always been on the left.

00:57:54.904 --> 00:57:57.340 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I've heard these
people demonize

00:57:57.340 --> 00:57:58.942 align:start size:84% position:16%
the people you're
not meant to talk to.

00:57:58.942 --> 00:58:00.176
I've heard them
mischaracterized.

00:58:00.176 --> 00:58:02.378 align:start size:84% position:16%
And then now, doing
what I'm doing,

00:58:02.378 --> 00:58:04.380 line:0%
a lotta conservatives like
what I do, which is great,

00:58:04.380 --> 00:58:07.450 line:0%
and you meet them and
they're really great.

00:58:07.450 --> 00:58:08.751 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
And some of the
people in particular

00:58:08.751 --> 00:58:10.720 line:0%
who I've been told
steer clear from,

00:58:10.720 --> 00:58:12.856 line:0%
have turned out to be just
the sweetest, nicest people,

00:58:12.856 --> 00:58:15.058 align:start size:88% position:13%
and they're nothing
like the public persona.

00:58:15.058 --> 00:58:17.827
And the irony is some of
my friends that I've lost

00:58:17.827 --> 00:58:21.965 align:start size:97% position:3%
who are famous lefties have
turned out to be the monsters.

00:58:21.965 --> 00:58:24.601
They've turned out to be the
bigots, the ones who will...

00:58:24.601 --> 00:58:26.069 align:start size:84% position:16%
I had one guy shouting
at me in a bar,

00:58:26.069 --> 00:58:27.770 align:start size:84% position:16%
calling me a Nazi
over and over again,

00:58:27.770 --> 00:58:30.573
and I'm thinking, I mean,
you're not a good person.

00:58:32.775 --> 00:58:35.778
It's really sad, but
I did this conference

00:58:35.778 --> 00:58:37.213
in London recently
with Peter Boghossian

00:58:37.213 --> 00:58:38.381 align:start size:84% position:16%
and James Lindsay
and Helen Pluckrose,

00:58:38.381 --> 00:58:39.749 align:start size:88% position:13%
which this was something
that was organized

00:58:39.749 --> 00:58:42.185 align:start size:97% position:3%
by a group called Sovereign
Nations who are...

00:58:42.185 --> 00:58:44.954 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's run by a guy
who's, Michael O'Fallon,

00:58:44.954 --> 00:58:49.092
who is a evangelical
Christian, right-wing.

00:58:49.092 --> 00:58:50.360
- Pete told me he
couldn't believe

00:58:50.360 --> 00:58:51.594
he was doing an event like this,

00:58:51.594 --> 00:58:53.129 align:start size:84% position:16%
he said yet these
people were amazing.

00:58:53.129 --> 00:58:56.299
- And such a nice guy though,
and then you get to the event,

00:58:56.299 --> 00:58:57.834
and I'm sitting there at lunch

00:58:57.834 --> 00:58:59.536 align:start size:84% position:16%
with the head of
the Atheist Society,

00:58:59.536 --> 00:59:02.939
next to an evangelical pastor,

00:59:02.939 --> 00:59:04.707
left-wing people,
right-wing people,

00:59:04.707 --> 00:59:06.609
Muslim, Christian, atheist,

00:59:06.609 --> 00:59:09.946
and you just think this
is what's happening now.

00:59:09.946 --> 00:59:11.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's people are finding
these alliances of people.

00:59:11.681 --> 00:59:13.149
It's not about left
and right now, right?

00:59:13.149 --> 00:59:14.417
We have to get rid of that.

00:59:14.417 --> 00:59:16.119
It's about if you
believe in liberty

00:59:16.119 --> 00:59:17.787
or if you want authority
figures to run everything,

00:59:17.787 --> 00:59:19.289
so it's liberty
versus authority,

00:59:19.289 --> 00:59:21.090 align:start size:97% position:3%
which is something that John
Stuart Mill talked about.

00:59:21.090 --> 00:59:22.759
That's where the alliances come.

00:59:22.759 --> 00:59:24.561
It's people who want freedom.

00:59:24.561 --> 00:59:27.030 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I think it doesn't
matter if you're right-wing

00:59:27.030 --> 00:59:30.066
or left-wing or whatever,
if you believe in that,

00:59:30.066 --> 00:59:31.367 align:start size:84% position:16%
then we've got
something in common

00:59:31.367 --> 00:59:32.869
and we can talk about that.

00:59:32.869 --> 00:59:35.038
And the other thing is we
all have to get together

00:59:35.038 --> 00:59:36.973 align:start size:88% position:13%
and work for this,
because if we lose that,

00:59:36.973 --> 00:59:38.975
we can't have all the other
conversations we wanna have

00:59:38.975 --> 00:59:40.310
about abortion,
about gay rights,

00:59:40.310 --> 00:59:42.245 align:start size:84% position:16%
about whatever, 'cause
nothing happens.

00:59:42.245 --> 00:59:44.380
If you don't have freedom
of speech, you got nothing.

00:59:44.380 --> 00:59:46.549
- I often say it, I don't
know what it says about me,

00:59:46.549 --> 00:59:49.586 align:start size:88% position:13%
but I have "On Liberty"
in my nightstand.

00:59:49.586 --> 00:59:51.087 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Do you?
- I have a little copy of it.

00:59:51.087 --> 00:59:52.055 align:start size:75% position:25%
- It's readable.
- Yeah.

00:59:52.055 --> 00:59:53.323
- It's totally readable.

00:59:53.323 --> 00:59:54.490
I think people are
intimidated by it

00:59:54.490 --> 00:59:55.658 align:start size:84% position:16%
because it was written
a long time ago,

00:59:55.658 --> 00:59:56.960 align:start size:81% position:19%
but it's readable.
- It's thin.

00:59:56.960 --> 00:59:58.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
- It's thin.
- It's thinner than this.

00:59:58.861 --> 01:00:00.496 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Well, no, it's quite
big font, but yeah.

01:00:00.496 --> 01:00:01.731
(Dave laughing)

01:00:01.731 --> 01:00:03.366
It's thin, it's great,
it's intersectional,

01:00:03.366 --> 01:00:04.968 align:start size:84% position:16%
because his wife
helped him write it,

01:00:04.968 --> 01:00:06.803 align:start size:88% position:13%
which she often
doesn't get credit for.

01:00:06.803 --> 01:00:07.971
There's a lot going
on in that book,

01:00:07.971 --> 01:00:09.672
and it's articulately expressed,

01:00:09.672 --> 01:00:14.677 align:start position:0%
and we need to get back to
those core principles of liberty

01:00:15.878 --> 01:00:17.013
and that should be
the standard point

01:00:17.013 --> 01:00:18.247 align:start size:88% position:13%
is that you are allowed
to argue with me

01:00:18.247 --> 01:00:19.482
and disagree and say
whatever you want.

01:00:19.482 --> 01:00:21.351
You can't arrest me,
you can't beat me up,

01:00:21.351 --> 01:00:23.286
and that should be the limit.

01:00:23.286 --> 01:00:25.321 align:start size:97% position:3%
But people don't agree
with that anymore, do they?

01:00:25.321 --> 01:00:27.423
- Andrew Doyle, you
are a true radical.

01:00:27.423 --> 01:00:28.691
(Andrew laughing)

01:00:28.691 --> 01:00:31.127
And I don't know that I
can have you back here.

01:00:31.127 --> 01:00:32.362
- Too controversial?

01:00:32.362 --> 01:00:33.630
Too hot to the touch?
- Too controversial,

01:00:33.630 --> 01:00:35.298
but we'll see, maybe.

01:00:35.298 --> 01:00:37.834
I'm gonna have to see what the
Twitterati thinks about this.

01:00:37.834 --> 01:00:39.035 align:start size:81% position:19%
- I know what they
think about me.

01:00:39.035 --> 01:00:40.303
- Should we send people?

01:00:40.303 --> 01:00:41.804 line:0%
I always send people
to a Twitter account,

01:00:41.804 --> 01:00:43.373 line:0%
but I don't know,
Titania's or...

01:00:43.373 --> 01:00:44.741 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
- Well, it depends
what you want.

01:00:44.741 --> 01:00:46.075 line:0%
If you wanna send
abuse, go to me.

01:00:46.075 --> 01:00:48.177 line:0%
That's andrewdoyle_com.

01:00:48.177 --> 01:00:49.979 line:0%
And if you wanna go for Titania,

01:00:49.979 --> 01:00:50.847 align:start size:84% position:16%
she's @TitaniaMcGrath,
simple as that.

01:00:53.683 --> 01:00:54.651
- He brought it to a close.

